From: Illia Komsa <ik@fungamer.co>
Subject: [PATCH] LibWeb: reorder line fragments across elements and fonts

The line box ordered glyph runs only inside one fragment, and a fragment
holds one text node's runs in one font. Fragments of different elements or
fonts were laid out in logical order, left to right even in a right-to-left
paragraph: Arabic words in two spans, a span inside an Arabic word, a number
or "%" in another font inside Arabic, and every multi-element line of a
dir=rtl block came out in the wrong order.

Merge a glyph run into a fragment only while its resolved direction holds,
so every fragment has one direction, and after the line is built resolve
each fragment's embedding level from its direction and its neighbours (W4,
W5, W7, N1, N2, I1, I2 over whole fragments; no explicit embeddings or
isolates) and reverse the fragments level by level (UAX #9 rule L2). The
fragments keep their logical order; their inline offsets move, and the
space between them (inline box edges, text-indent) moves with the run it is
inside. Justification spreads space in visual order on reordered lines.

---
diff --git a/Libraries/LibWeb/Rust/src/layout/inline_formatting_context.rs b/Libraries/LibWeb/Rust/src/layout/inline_formatting_context.rs
index fec5c04bad..b7ea372118 100644
--- a/Libraries/LibWeb/Rust/src/layout/inline_formatting_context.rs
+++ b/Libraries/LibWeb/Rust/src/layout/inline_formatting_context.rs
@@ -337,8 +337,15 @@ pub(crate) fn apply_to_fragments(text_justify: u8, line: &mut line_box::LineBoxD
         CssPixels::default()
     };
 
+    // Spread the space from left to right: in visual order, which differs from the logical one where line_bidi
+    // reordered the fragments.
+    let mut visual_order: Vec<usize> = (0..line.fragments.len()).collect();
+    if line.is_visually_reordered {
+        visual_order.sort_by_key(|index| line.fragments[*index].inline_offset);
+    }
     let mut running_diff = CssPixels::default();
-    for fragment in &mut line.fragments {
+    for index in visual_order {
+        let fragment = &mut line.fragments[index];
         if fragment.is_fully_truncated {
             continue;
         }
@@ -1349,6 +1356,7 @@ impl<'context> InlineFormattingContext<'context> {
                     .collect(),
                 static_position_markers: Vec::new(),
                 inline_box_baselines: Vec::new(),
+                is_visually_reordered: false,
             };
             fragment_start = fragment_end;
             let line_item_start = item_index;
